1
00:00:00,435 --> 00:00:04,354
Recognizing an answer is different from explaining why it works.

2
00:00:04,614 --> 00:00:08,533
Dekisugi-kun turns science study into teaching a companion.

3
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:14,703
For middle and high-school learners, each mission starts with a concrete question.

4
00:00:14,964 --> 00:00:17,561
I predict that the heavier ball falls faster.

5
00:00:19,168 --> 00:00:23,759
The lesson explains why both balls fall together, and when that claim holds.

6
00:00:25,368 --> 00:00:29,588
Then the material disappears. I must explain it in my own words.

7
00:00:29,849 --> 00:00:33,003
Typing is a full learning route, alongside voice.

8
00:00:34,601 --> 00:00:38,242
Key-term coverage prompts reflection, not a mastery score.

9
00:00:38,503 --> 00:00:42,213
A fixed follow-up asks me to apply the idea to a new case.

10
00:00:43,801 --> 00:00:47,164
My wrong choice brings a hint about the vacuum condition.

11
00:00:47,425 --> 00:00:51,691
I rethink my explanation instead of receiving an answer to copy.

12
00:00:53,301 --> 00:00:58,380
The companion's record keeps uncertain ideas for a matching repair activity.

13
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:01,817
Rewriting alone does not mark an idea corrected.

14
00:01:03,435 --> 00:01:05,870
The core works offline, without an account.

15
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:11,325
Student explanations are neither uploaded nor graded by an external AI.

16
00:01:12,935 --> 00:01:18,129
RevenueCat powers optional Plus, with companion styling and parent reports.

17
00:01:18,390 --> 00:01:24,048
Here is a completed Test Store purchase. No real charge, and core lessons stay free.

18
00:01:25,635 --> 00:01:28,649
Twelve science units. Thirty-five concepts.

19
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:31,971
Dekisugi-kun. Make explaining part of studying.

